    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="32">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 32</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="32" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="102" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXVI. Gif Wilisc mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_32.lnote.oe.17"/> hæbbe hide<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_32.lnote.oe.18"/> londes, his wer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_32.lnote.oe.19-2"/> bið CXX scill.; gif he þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> healfes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_32.lnote.oe.20-2"/> hæbbe, LXXX scill.; gif<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Ine_32.lnote.oe.21"/> he nænig hæbbe, LX scillinga.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="32" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="102" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXVI. Gif Wilisc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_32.lnote.oe.9"/> mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_32.lnote.oe.2"/> hæbbe hide londes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_32.lnote.oe.10"/>, his wer bið CXX scll'; gif he þonne hæbbe healfes, LXXX scll'; gif he nænig næbbe, LX scillinga.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="32" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="102" ed="#liebermann"/>Be Wylisces mannes landhæfene. Gyf Wylisc man hæbbe hide landes, his wer bið hundtwelftig scill'; gyf he ðonne healfe hæbbe, hundeahtati scill'; gyf he næbbe nan land, sixti scill'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="32" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="103" ed="#liebermann"/>Si homo Waliscus habeat hidam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_32.lnote.oe.19"/> terrę, wera sua<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_32.lnote.oe.20"/> est centum uiginti solid., si dimidiam habeat, LXXX sol., si nullam habeat, LX sol.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="46" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be Wylisces mannes landhæfene.] Gif Wilisc mon hæbbe hide londes, his wer bið CXX scill.; gif he þonne healfes<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#Ine_32.attnote.fn.8"/> hæbbe, LXXX scill.; gif he nænig hæbbe<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#Ine_32.attnote.fn.9"/>, LX scillinga.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="32" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="398" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LXXVI} Gif Wiliscmon hæbbe hide londes, his wer bið CXX sciƚƚ; gif he þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> healfes hæbbe, LXXX sciƚƚ; gif he nænig hæbbe, LX scillinga.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_32.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="103" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn ein Wälscher Mann [1] Hide Landes besitzt, beträgt sein Wergeld 120 Schill.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_32.lnote.de.2"/>; wenn er aber ein halbes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_32.lnote.de.3"/> [Hufenland] besitzt, 80 Schill.; wenn er kein [Land] hat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_32.lnote.de.4"/>, 60<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_32.lnote.de.5"/> Schillinge.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a Welshman possesses [1] hide of land, his wergeld is 120 shillings; but if he possesses half [a hide of land], 80 shillings; if he has no [land], 60 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="47" ed="#attenborough"/>If a Welshman possesses a hide of land, his wergeld shall be 120 shillings<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_32.attnote.n.1"/>. If, however, he possesses half a hide, his wergeld shall be 80 shillings; if he possesses no land—60 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="403" ed="#whitelock"/>If a Welshman has a hide of land, his wergild is 120 shillings; if, however, he has a half hide, 80 shillings; if he has none, 60 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="399" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a Welshman has a hide of land, his <hi rend="italic">wer</hi> is 120 shillings; if he, however, has half, 80 shillings; if he has none, 60 shillings.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:Northleoda_7">Norðleoda 7</ref>; <ref target="clause:Northleoda_7-1">Norðleoda 7.1</ref>; <ref target="clause:Northleoda_8">Norðleoda 8</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="398"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_24-2">Ine 24.2</ref> <quote>Compare to §23.1.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="399"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_23-3">Ine 23.3</ref> <quote>Cf. Ine §23 and note.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="399"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Northleoda_8">Norðleoda 8</ref> <quote>Cf. Norðleoda Laga (§8) which Liebermann dates 920–954. The later text adds here and þeah freo sie</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="391"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_23-3">Ine 23.3</ref> <quote>§32 sets the wergild of a Welshman who owns no property – that is, a hired worker – at 60 shillings.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="390"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_24-2">Ine 24.2</ref> <quote>it has clearly been misplaced by scribal error [...] Compare §32.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="419"><label>see</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_54-1">Ine 54.1</ref> <quote>The value of a Welsh slave was 50 shillings (see §32 and note)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="394"><label>derives from</label> <ref target="clause:Northleoda_7">Norðleoda 7–12</ref> <quote>the author looked up Ine's law on 'Welsh' status for guidance in a northern society</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="367"><label>likely reference to</label> <ref target="clause:Northleoda_7">Norðleoda 7</ref> <quote>Likely references include [...] Norðleoda laga §§7 (Ine §32)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="367"><label>likely reference to</label> <ref target="clause:Grith_7">Grið 7</ref> <quote>Likely references include [...] Grið §7 (Ine §32)</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_32.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hyd. <hi rend="italic">T;</hi> t. h. <hi rend="italic">M Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hyd. T; t. h. M Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_32.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eius <hi rend="italic">ohne</hi> est <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eius without est Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_32.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">zweites</hi> i <hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">second i written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_32.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_32.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a; es <hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a; es written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_32.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">man <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">man Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_32.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hyde lan. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hyde lan. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_32.lnote.oe.19-2" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">were biþ hund twelftig <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">were biþ hund twelftig Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_32.lnote.oe.20-2" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-fe h., eahtatig <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-fe h., eahtatig Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_32.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">diesen Satz bringt Ld unter Errata:</hi> gif he næbbe nán land, 60 s.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ld gives this sentence under Errata: gif he næbbe nán land, 60 s.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_32.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Scheint benutzt von Norðleod 7f. — <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Hufe 5a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Seems to have been used by Norðleod 7f. — <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Hufe 5a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_32.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o.</hi> 23, 3. 24, 2; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Walliser 3a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> 23, 3. 24, 2; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Walliser 3a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_32.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dass <hi rend="italic">hid</hi> nicht immer fem. (wonach Sweet <hi rend="italic">Reader: healfe</hi> ändern wollte), <hi rend="italic">s. Wb,</hi> auch Urk. Bi 558</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">That <hi rend="italic">hid</hi> is not always fem. (on which ground Sweet <hi rend="italic">Reader</hi> wished to emend to <hi rend="italic">healfe</hi>): <hi rend="italic">see Wb,</hi> also the charter Bi 558</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_32.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘kein Land’ B. — ‘jedoch frei ist’ fügt Norðleod 8 hinzu, vielleicht weil 60 Schill. auch Sklavenpreis ist</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘no land’ B. — Norðleod 8 adds ‘but is free’, perhaps because 60 shill. is also the price of a slave</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_32.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Wergeld 19; Stand 7. a; Grundbesitz 7. 8</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Wergeld 19; Stand 7. a; Grundbesitz 7. 8</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_32.attnote.fn.8" n="8" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><label>healfes</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">healfe</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_32.attnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><label>hæbbe</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">næbbe nan land</hi>. B. <hi rend="italic">nænig næbbe</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_32.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">186</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. <hi rend="italic">Northleoda Laga</hi>, cap. 7 f. From a comparison between this law and cap. 23 § 2 above, it may perhaps be inferred that the <hi rend="italic">gafolgelda</hi> still commonly possessed a hide of land.</seg></note>
      </div>
